venv/
logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
*.session

# The person lives in $HERALD_HOME (~/.herald by default), which is its own
# private repository: config.json, secrets.json, the ledger and any extensions.
# `ledger` here is a symlink into it, so every prompt, skill and docstring can
# go on saying `ledger/identity/` and be right, while none of it is ever
# tracked by the program's repository.
/ledger

# Generated by `herald constitution` from config/constitution.md plus the
# personal half in the ledger. See lib/herald/constitution.py.
/CLAUDE.md

# Generated by `herald ext sync` from config/claude-settings.base.json plus
# every enabled extension's hooks.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Symlinks written by `herald ext sync`. They point at absolute paths inside
# this machine's $HERALD_HOME, so tracking them would publish the names of
# somebody's private extensions along with their username.
.claude/skills/
config/herald.json
config/secrets.json
secrets/

# Each project is its own repository.
projects/*/
!projects/README.md
